<!--Post: 8307--><!--Time: 1109047020-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8307"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Neechi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Neechi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 8:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->On KAKE&#39;s website they are running a banner for a story tomorrow at 10pm. It says BTK&#39;s 9th Victim?  Anyone have any idea what they are referring to?  Has anyone else heard anything like this? <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kake.com/" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8307-->
<!--Post: 8309--><!--Time: 1109047775-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8309"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 8:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Melissa Scott! <BR> <BR><a href="http://forums.prospero.com/foxamw/messages" target=_top>http://forums.prospero.com/foxamw/messages</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8309-->
<!--Post: 8312--><!--Time: 1109049040-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8312"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 9:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->a poster at Kansas.com says it is Delores Dee Davis<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8312-->
<!--Post: 8314--><!--Time: 1109049587-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8314"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Neechi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Neechi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 9:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Probably it&#39;s going to end up being yet another warm and fuzzy human interest story and be about a victim that wasn&#39;t a direct victim, but their life was ruined by BTK.  KAKE is notorious for sensationalist journalism under the best of circumstances, so who knows if they are actually going to say anything worth a crap or just be yet another ratings grabber.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8314-->
<!--Post: 8315--><!--Time: 1109050223-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8315"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Icyou<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Icyou<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 9:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->They are going to have Dee Davis&#39; son on because he believes his mother was a victim of BTK.  He will tell his story.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8315-->
<!--Post: 8335--><!--Time: 1109058063-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8335"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Kansasgirl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Kansasgirl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 11:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I noticed on the previews that the son mentions a partially eaten bowl of cereal. Who knows. KAKE just keeps dragging on with stories that are void of information.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8335-->
<!--Post: 8385--><!--Time: 1109100994-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8385"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 11:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->From KAKE News today at 11:30 am: <BR> <BR>Jemelle Holopirek: The list of confirmed BTK victims could get longer as police get more clues from the killer, and one man is wondering if his mother was one of the victims. 62 year old &#34;Dee&#34; Davis was strangled fourteen years ago, her bound body found under a northern Sedgwick County bridge. Davis&#39; son Jeff said several items were missing from his mother&#39;s home after the murder. He spoke out in an exclusive interview with our KAKE On Your Side investigative reporter Jeff Golimowsky, where he is calling on BTK to end the speculation. <BR> <BR>Jeff Davis: ...playing cat and mouse with everybody. Show me if you&#39;ve got it. Show me you do, &#39;cause I don&#39;t believe it. So, prove it to me and... <BR> <BR>Jemelle Holopirek: And we&#39;ll have much more from our On Your Side investigation in our exclusive interview with Jeff Davis tonight, including never before released details about the Davis murder. Could she be BTK&#39;s 9th Victim? Be sure to watch this KAKE News exclusive tonight at 10. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8385-->
<!--Post: 8406--><!--Time: 1109113845-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8406"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 3:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I got a mail form someone who believes Melissa is the same girl that worked for him two years ago, any way we could find a PIC. to varify?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8406-->
<!--Post: 8410--><!--Time: 1109115438-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8410"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 3:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Things missing from the Davis house, could it be.......jewelry, and maybe a box of cereal? Who would even notice if a box of their mothers cereal was missing. <BR>Maybe drop #7? <BR>This is too weird, if it was &#34;the souless one&#34; who ended Delores&#39; life, he has had this cereal thing planned out since 1991, eating some and leaving it in the sink. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8410-->
<!--Post: 8412--><!--Time: 1109115900-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8412"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 3:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Remember when I said that Dee and some other woman both died after eating in the same restaurant in Park City. BTW there were a few more bodys dumped in that area around the time, these two were killed.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8412-->
<!--Post: 8446--><!--Time: 1109134412-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8446"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 8:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The story said that a broach &#40;jewelry&#41;, a camera and her dirver&#39;s liscence were what ws missing from Mrs. Davis&#39; house. These are the 3 MOST obvious items for BTK to take. His photography thing with taking pictures at each murder scene, his interest in jewelry, and his obvious taking of DL&#39;s from his victims make it pretty obvious that we are looking at number 9 - Mrs. Davis.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8446-->
<!--Post: 8448--><!--Time: 1109134631-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8448"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 8:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Besides the missing camera, brooch and DL, the killer had signs of ritualistic behaviors: phone cut, strangled and bound, bowl of cereal in sink, car keys thrown on roof, shoes piled in pyramids, not brick but large concrete masonry block thrown at house to break glass.  <BR>-Deb  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8448-->
<!--Post: 8461--><!--Time: 1109149833-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8461"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hackenmaster@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 1:10 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->flytodeb-they never said large concrete masonry block.  <BR> <BR>Embersage-I would agree with you he is a great planner if he took the cereal box after eating a bowl.  Lets thin k about that for a minute, why wouldnt the police follow up on, well here is a bowl of cereal in the sink.....wheres the box?  I would think they would have looked in the cabinet, or atleast in the trash to verify that infact THERE WAS CEREAL IN THE HOUSE, and nows theres not.  And indeed that would be very well planned out. <BR> <BR>The simple fact that it was a cereal box, with a brick on the top, in Park City none the less, I feel BTK might be getting tired of WPD giving all his trophies and letters to the FBI for verification......So he thought to himself...If i write a letter to KAKE they will get there first and guranteed they would film and snap off shots, before police were notified.  The police show up...you can show this one this one and this one.  So what did the public get?  A cereal box, a brick, Park City, Jewelry &#40;broach&#41;...Was he in his own way giving Joe Public a clue too? <BR> <BR>Thats my story and Im stickin to it! <BR> <BR>wichitan <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8461-->
<!--Post: 8470--><!--Time: 1109166109-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8470"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:BTK_Catcher@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Catcher<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Catcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 5:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;They&#34; never said large concrete masonry block, but Davis&#39; son said large concrete masonry block.  I definitely agree with flytodeb that he stated that in the interview.  In fact he added something along the lines of it being big and heavy enough to question why one would go through the trouble of using that just to break the window.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8470-->
<!--Post: 8486--><!--Time: 1109174857-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8486"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 8:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Delores Dee Davis, 6226 N. hillside, Park City, 1-19-91, Died after eating in same Restaurant as another unsolved murder victim, Marin Hedge.  COD strangulation,, found under a bridge, at 3600 block of 117Th st n.   near Meridian in Norther Sedgewick, Had cut her phone lines. <BR>Interesting that there are a few other unsolved murders in the same area with the same MO that had been dumped on the side of the roads.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8486-->
<!--Post: 8524--><!--Time: 1109183451-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8524"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 10:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here is the link to the interview with &#34;Dee&#34; Davis&#39; son Jeff Davis. You can also watch the video. Ok, I said &#34;large&#34; concrete masonry block. I exaggerated when I said large. What he said was &#34;It was not a brick, it was a concrete masonry block, big heavy block.&#34; Sorry for telling you the wrong thing. <BR>-Deb <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/1296247.html" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/1296247.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8524-->
<!--Post: 8676--><!--Time: 1109280291-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8676"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 1:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If they find out that BTK did send them a piece from Dees home, that is going to open a new can of worms, because that would mean he could be responsible for up to seven other murders in that area at the same time<!--/Text--></td></tr>
